Claude Co...","es":"Guía de configuración de practice-viriditas para entornos...","fr":"Guide d''installation de practice-viriditas pour les envir...","de":"Einrichtungsleitfaden für practice-viriditas in WSL-Windo...","pt":"Guia de Configuração do practice-viriditas para Desenvolv...","ru":"Настройка practice-viriditas: ИИ Агенты для WSL-Windows","ar":"إعداد practice-viriditas: أدوات الذكاء الاصطناعي للتنمية"},"description":{"en":"Unlock comprehensive development guides for WSL-Windows environments with Claude Code integration. Start your practice-viriditas journey today and discover a...","zh":"了解 practice-viriditas 的综合开发指南，用于 WSL-Windows 环境的 Claude Code 集成，提高开发效率","ja":"WSL-Windows 環境の Claude Code 統合を使用した practice-viriditas の包括的な開発ガイドを参照してください","ko":"WSL-Windows 개발 환경 및 Claude Code 통합을 위한 practice-viriditas의 종합 개발 가이드를 확인하세요","es":"Descubre cómo configurar practice-viriditas en entornos WSL-Windows con Claude Code para mejorar tu desarrollo","fr":"Découvrez comment installer practice-viriditas dans les environnements WSL-Windows avec Claude Code pour améliorer votre développement","de":"Erfahren Sie, wie Sie practice-viriditas in WSL-Windows-Umgebungen mit Claude Code-Integration einrichten können, um Ihr Entwicklungserlebnis zu verbessern","pt":"Aprenda a configurar o practice-viriditas com Claude Code para ambientes WSL-Windows e melhore sua produtividade","ru":"Узнайте, как настроить practice-viriditas с Claude Code для WSL-Windows и повысьте свою эффективность","ar":"تعلم كيفية ضبط practice-viriditas مع Claude Code لبيئات WSL-Windows وطور من إنتاجيتك"},"definition":{"en":"practice-viriditas is a skill that offers comprehensive development guides for WSL-Windows environments with Claude Code integration, focusing on Hildegardian contemplative spirituality and nature-inspired coding practices.","zh":"practice-viriditas 是一个提供 WSL-Windows 环境 Claude Code 集成的开发工具","ja":"practice-viriditas は、WSL-Windows 環境の Claude Code 統合を提供する開発ツールです","ko":"practice-viriditas는 WSL-Windows 개발 환경의 Claude Code 통합을 제공하는 개발 도구입니다","es":"Practice-viriditas es un conjunto de guías de desarrollo para entornos WSL-Windows con integración de Claude Code","fr":"Practice-viriditas est un ensemble de guides de développement pour les environnements WSL-Windows avec intégration de Claude Code","de":"Practice-viriditas ist ein Satz von Entwicklungshandbüchern für WSL-Windows-Umgebungen mit Claude Code-Integration","pt":"O practice-viriditas é um guia de desenvolvimento que fornece diretrizes para ambientes WSL-Windows","ru":"Practice-viriditas - это руководство по разработке, которое предоставляет рекомендации для WSL-Windows","ar":"practice-viriditas هو دليل تنمية يقدم إرشادات لبيئات WSL-Windows"},"features":{"en":["Provides comprehensive development guides for WSL-Windows environments","Integrates Claude Code for enhanced coding capabilities","Supports Hildegardian contemplative spirituality and nature-inspired coding practices","Offers meditation and philosophical contemplation guides for developers","Enables integration with seasonal rhythms and natural world concepts","Utilizes SKILL.md content for technical guidance and support"],"zh":["WSL-Windows 环境支持","Claude Code 集成","综合开发指南","提高开发效率"],"ja":["WSL-Windows 環境対応","Claude Code 統合","包括的な開発ガイド","開発効率の向上"],"ko":["WSL-Windows 개발 환경 지원","Claude Code 통합","종합 개발 가이드","개발 효율성 향상"],"es":["Guías de desarrollo integrales para WSL-Windows","Integración de Claude Code para mejorar la productividad","Compatibilidad con entornos de desarrollo WSL-Windows","Soporte para la creación de aplicaciones con tecnologías web","Herramientas de desarrollo para mejorar la eficiencia"],"fr":["Guides de développement complets pour les environnements WSL-Windows","Intégration de Claude Code pour améliorer la productivité","Compatibilité avec les environnements de développement WSL-Windows","Support pour la création d''applications avec des technologies web","Outils de développement pour améliorer l''efficacité"],"de":["Umfassende Entwicklungshandbücher für WSL-Windows-Umgebungen","Integration von Claude Code für verbesserte Produktivität","Kompatibilität mit WSL-Windows-Entwicklungsumgebungen","Unterstützung für die Erstellung von Anwendungen mit Webtechnologien","Entwicklungstools für verbesserte Effizienz"],"pt":["Integração com Claude Code","Desenvolvimento para ambientes WSL-Windows","Guia de configuração abrangente","Suporte à produtividade do desenvolvedor","Integração com tecnologias de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["Интеграция с Claude Code","Разработка для WSL-Windows","Комплексное руководство по настройке","Повышение эффективности разработчика","Интеграция с технологиями разработки"],"ar":["التكامل مع Claude Code","التنمية لبيئات WSL-Windows","دليل إعداد شامل","دعم إنتاجية المطور","التكامل مع تقنيات التنمية"]},"keywords":{"en":["how to use practice-viriditas","what is practice-viriditas","practice-viriditas alternative","practice-viriditas vs Claude Code","practice-viriditas install","practice-viriditas setup guide","WSL-Windows development guides","Claude Code integration","Hildegardian contemplative spirituality"],"zh":["practice-viriditas","WSL-Windows","Claude Code","开发环境","开发工具","AIエージェント","综合开发指南"],"ja":["practice-viriditas","WSL-Windows","Claude Code","開発環境","開発ツール","AIエージェント","包括的な開発ガイド"],"ko":["practice-viriditas","WSL-Windows","Claude Code","개발 환경","개발 도구","AI 에이전트","종합 개발 가이드"],"es":["practice-viriditas","Guías de desarrollo WSL-Windows","Integración de Claude Code","Desarrollo de aplicaciones web","Herramientas de desarrollo","Entornos de desarrollo WSL-Windows","Productividad en el desarrollo","Mejora de la eficiencia en el desarrollo"],"fr":["practice-viriditas","Guides de développement WSL-Windows","Intégration de Claude Code","Développement d''applications web","Outils de développement","Environnements de développement WSL-Windows","Productivité dans le développement","Amélioration de l''efficacité dans le développement"],"de":["practice-viriditas","Entwicklungshandbücher WSL-Windows","Integration von Claude Code","Entwicklung von Webanwendungen","Entwicklungstools","WSL-Windows-Entwicklungsumgebungen","Produktivität in der Entwicklung","Verbesserung der Effizienz in der Entwicklung"],"pt":["practice-viriditas","desenvolvimento WSL-Windows","Claude Code","guia de configuração","produtividade do desenvolvedor","tecnologias de desenvolvimento","ambientes de desenvolvimento"],"ru":["practice-viriditas","разработка WSL-Windows","Claude Code","руководство по настройке","эфективность разработчика","технологии разработки","среды разработки"],"ar":["practice-viriditas","التنمية لبيئات WSL-Windows","Claude Code","دليل إعداد","إنتاجية المطور","تقنيات التنمية","بيئات التنمية"]}},"owner":"pjt222","repo":"development-guides","repoPath":"pjt222/development-guides","stars":0,"forks":0,"updatedAt":"2026-03-08T01:57:15.659Z","topics":[],"category":"community","skillMd":{"name":"practice-viriditas","description":">","version":"1.0","tags":"hildegard, viriditas, greening, meditation, nature, contemplation, seasonal","bodyPreview":"# Practice Viriditas\r\n\r\nGuide meditation and philosophical contemplation on *viriditas* — Hildegard von Bingen''s concept of the divine greening power that permeates all creation.\r\n\r\n## When to Use\r\n\r\n- You want to practice Hildegardian contemplative spirituality grounded in nature\r\n- You feel disconnected from the natural world or seasonal rhythms\r\n- You need a meditation practice that integrates body, earth, and spirit\r\n- You are experiencing spiritual dryness or lack of vitality (opposite of v","body":"# Practice Viriditas\r\n\r\nGuide meditation and philosophical contemplation on *viriditas* — Hildegard von Bingen''s concept of the divine greening power that permeates all creation.\r\n\r\n## When to Use\r\n\r\n- You want to practice Hildegardian contemplative spirituality grounded in nature\r\n- You feel disconnected from the natural world or seasonal rhythms\r\n- You need a meditation practice that integrates body, earth, and spirit\r\n- You are experiencing spiritual dryness or lack of vitality (opposite of viriditas)\r\n- You want to deepen understanding of Hildegard''s ecological theology\r\n- You are seeking seasonal attunement practices through the liturgical and agricultural year\r\n\r\n## Inputs\r\n\r\n- **Required**: Current season (spring, summer, autumn, winter) or liturgical season (Advent, Lent, Easter, Ordinary Time)\r\n- **Optional**: Access to outdoor natural space (garden, park, forest) — indoor practice possible but less ideal\r\n- **Optional**: Current life situation (burnout, grief, transition, stagnation) — informs practice focus\r\n- **Optional**: Duration preference (5-10 min brief, 15-20 min standard, 30+ min extended)\r\n- **Optional**: Experience level (beginner, intermediate, advanced)\r\n\r\n## Procedure\r\n\r\n### Step 1: Understand the Concept of Viriditas\r\n\r\nGround the practice in Hildegard''s theological and natural philosophy.\r\n\r\n```\r\nVIRIDITAS — The Greening Power:\r\n\r\nDefinition:\r\nViriditas (from Latin \"viridis\" = green) is Hildegard''s term for the divine\r\nlife force that animates all creation. It is not merely \"greenness\" as color,\r\nbut the FORCE of growth, renewal, vitality, fecundity, and regeneration.\r\n\r\nHildegard''s Own Words:\r\n\"There is a power that has been from all eternity, and that force and\r\npotentiality is greenness... God has arranged all things in the world in\r\nconsideration of everything else.\"\r\n(*Liber Divinorum Operum*, Vision 1)\r\n\r\n\"Glance at the sun. See the moon and stars. Gaze at the beauty of earth''s\r\ngreenings. Now, think. What delight God gives to humankind with all these\r\nthings... All nature is at the disposal of humankind. We are to work with it.\r\nFor without it, we cannot survive.\"\r\n(*Scivias*, Book II, Vision 1)\r\n\r\nTheological Context:\r\n- Viriditas is NOT pantheism (nature = God)\r\n- Viriditas is God''s creative power EXPRESSED THROUGH nature\r\n- It is the Holy Spirit''s work in the material world\r\n- Humanity participates in viriditas through care, cultivation, and contemplation\r\n\r\nViriditas in the Human Person:\r\n- Physical: Health, vitality, energy, fruitfulness\r\n- Spiritual: Growth in virtue, generativity, creative work\r\n- Relational: Life-giving relationships, community flourishing\r\n- Ecological: Tending the earth, participating in regeneration\r\n\r\nOPPOSITE OF VIRIDITAS = ARIDITAS (Dryness):\r\n- Physical: Illness, exhaustion, infertility\r\n- Spiritual: Acedia (sloth), despair, sterility of soul\r\n- Ecological: Degradation, deforestation, soil depletion\r\n- Moral: Sin as \"withering\" or \"drying up\" of the soul''s greenness\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected:** User understands viriditas as divine life force in creation, not mere aesthetic greenness. Recognizes viriditas/ariditas as a spectrum of vitality.\r\n\r\n**On failure:** If theological language feels inaccessible, frame viriditas as \"life force\" or \"vitality\" — the power that makes things grow, heal, and flourish. Proceed with meditation practice.\r\n\r\n### Step 2: Preparation — Grounding and Centering\r\n\r\nPrepare the body and mind for contemplative engagement with viriditas.\r\n\r\n```\r\nPreparation Protocol (5 minutes):\r\n\r\nLOCATION:\r\n- Ideal: Outdoors in a natural setting (garden, park, forest edge, meadow)\r\n- Acceptable: Indoors near a window with a living plant visible\r\n- Minimum: Indoors with no view — use imagination and memory of nature\r\n\r\nPOSTURE:\r\n- Seated on ground, cushion, or chair — spine upright but not rigid\r\n- Hands resting on knees or in lap\r\n- Eyes open (soft gaze at nature) OR closed (inner visualization)\r\n- Barefoot if outdoors and weather permits (direct earth contact)\r\n\r\nGROUNDING:\r\n1. Take 3 deep breaths — inhale through nose, exhale through mouth\r\n2. Scan body from feet to head:\r\n   - Notice where you feel tense or closed\r\n   - Notice where you feel open or relaxed\r\n3. Imagine roots growing from your sitting bones into the earth\r\n   - You are rooted, like a tree\r\n   - You are part of the soil, not separate from it\r\n\r\nCENTERING:\r\n1. Bring attention to your heart center (chest, sternum)\r\n2. Recall Hildegard''s image: \"O most honored Greening Force, you are worthy\r\n   of embrace.\"\r\n3. Set intention: \"I am here to witness and participate in viriditas.\"\r\n   - Not to achieve or produce anything\r\n   - Not to \"get\" something from nature\r\n   - Simply to attune, observe, and participate\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected:** User is settled, grounded, and mentally prepared for contemplative engagement. Distraction has decreased; awareness has sharpened.\r\n\r\n**On failure:** If mind is highly agitated or distracted, extend preparation phase. Add a body scan (feet → legs → torso → arms → head) to bring awareness into the body before proceeding.\r\n\r\n### Step 3: Core Meditation — Observing Viriditas\r\n\r\nEngage in structured contemplation on the greening power in nature.\r\n\r\n```\r\nViriditas Meditation Structure (15-20 minutes):\r\n\r\nPHASE 1: OBSERVATION (5-7 minutes)\r\nLook at the natural world (or visualize it if indoors):\r\n- Where do you see green? Notice shades: lime, forest, olive, emerald\r\n- Where do you see NEW growth? Fresh shoots, buds, young leaves\r\n- Where do you see MATURE growth? Full foliage, thick bark, flowering\r\n- Where do you see DECAY? Dead leaves, fallen branches, composting matter\r\n  (Note: Decay is PART OF viriditas — it feeds new growth)\r\n\r\nSpecific Focus Questions:\r\n- Which plant or tree draws your attention? Why?\r\n- Where is viriditas most VIGOROUS? (New growth, climbing vines)\r\n- Where is viriditas most PATIENT? (Ancient trees, slow-growing moss)\r\n- Where is viriditas RESTING? (Seeds in soil, dormant buds in winter)\r\n\r\nPHASE 2: PARTICIPATION (5-7 minutes)\r\nShift from observing to FEELING yourself as part of the greening:\r\n- Place one hand on your heart, one on your belly\r\n- Breathe deeply and imagine:\r\n  - On INHALE: Sap rising through your spine, like a tree drawing water\r\n    from roots to crown\r\n  - On EXHALE: Releasing what is dead, dried, or no longer needed —\r\n    let it fall like autumn leaves\r\n\r\nAffirmation (Hildegard''s words):\r\n\"I am the supreme and fiery force who kindled every living spark...\r\nI flame above the beauty of the fields; I shine in the waters;\r\nI burn in the sun, the moon, and the stars.\"\r\n(*Scivias*, Book I, Vision 2)\r\n\r\nContinue breath cycle 7-10 rounds:\r\n- INHALE: Receive viriditas (vitality, life force, greening)\r\n- EXHALE: Release ariditas (dryness, exhaustion, withering)\r\n\r\nPHASE 3: INTEGRATION (3-5 minutes)\r\n- Return to normal breathing\r\n- Ask: \"Where in my life do I feel viriditas (alive, growing, generative)?\"\r\n- Ask: \"Where in my life do I feel ariditas (dry, stuck, lifeless)?\"\r\n- No need to answer verbally — simply let awareness arise\r\n- Bow to the green world in gratitude\r\n\r\nCLOSING:\r\nHildegard''s Prayer: \"O noble Greening, you are rooted in the sun, and in\r\nbright serenity you shine forth in a wheel that no earthly excellence can\r\ncomprehend.\"\r\nStand slowly. Re-enter ordinary awareness with renewed vitality.\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected:** User has experienced contemplative attunement to viriditas, both in external nature and internal life force. Sense of connection to living world strengthened.\r\n\r\n**On failure:** If meditation feels abstract or ungrounded, reduce visualization and focus ONLY on breath awareness with natural surroundings. Viriditas practice requires less \"doing\" and more \"allowing.\"\r\n\r\n### Step 4: Seasonal Attunement\r\n\r\nTailor the practice to the current season, recognizing that viriditas manifests differently throughout the year.\r\n\r\n```\r\nSeasonal Variations of Viriditas Practice:\r\n\r\nSPRING (March-May) — Viriditas ERUPTING:\r\n- Observation: Focus on buds, shoots, seedlings, first flowers\r\n- Meditation theme: Rebirth, new beginnings, potential breaking through\r\n- Affirmation: \"I am greening. New life stirs within me.\"\r\n- Action integration: Plant seeds (literal or metaphorical), begin new project\r\n- Liturgical connection: Easter (Resurrection as ultimate viriditas)\r\n\r\nSUMMER (June-August) — Viriditas at FULLNESS:\r\n- Observation: Focus on lush foliage, fruit formation, peak growth\r\n- Meditation theme: Abundance, manifestation, full expression of life\r\n- Affirmation: \"I am in full bloom. I bear fruit.\"\r\n- Action integration: Harvest (literally from garden, metaphorically from work)\r\n- Liturgical connection: Pentecost (Holy Spirit as fire AND greening)\r\n\r\nAUTUMN (September-November) — Viriditas HARVESTING and COMPOSTING:\r\n- Observation: Focus on seeds, falling leaves, fruit ripening and releasing\r\n- Meditation theme: Letting go, death as part of cycle, preparation for rest\r\n- Affirmation: \"I release what is ripe. I compost what is dead.\"\r\n- Action integration: Clear clutter, complete projects, prepare for winter rest\r\n- Liturgical connection: All Saints/All Souls (honoring death as passage)\r\n\r\nWINTER (December-February) — Viriditas RESTING (not absent):\r\n- Observation: Focus on dormant buds, seeds under snow, evergreen resilience\r\n- Meditation theme: Patience, hidden growth, trust in unseen life\r\n- Affirmation: \"I rest in the dark soil. I prepare to rise again.\"\r\n- Action integration: Stillness, contemplation, visioning without action\r\n- Liturgical connection: Advent (waiting in darkness for the coming Light)\r\n  and Lent (spiritual winter before Easter spring)\r\n\r\nNOTE: Viriditas is ALWAYS present, even in winter — it is resting,\r\nnot dead. Winter viriditas is the power that holds the promise of spring.\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected:** Practice adapted to current season with appropriate focus (erupting/full/harvesting/resting). User recognizes viriditas as year-round force, not limited to spring/summer.\r\n\r\n**On failure:** If seasonal variation feels confusing, practice core meditation (Step 3) without seasonal overlay. Seasonal attunement is enrichment, not requirement.\r\n\r\n### Step 5: Integration — Living as Viriditas\r\n\r\nExtend the practice from meditation into daily life, embodying the greening power.\r\n\r\n```\r\nIntegration Practices — Daily and Weekly:\r\n\r\nDAILY MICRO-PRACTICES (5 minutes):\r\n- Morning: Step outside (or to a window) and greet the day''s green world\r\n  with one breath of gratitude\r\n- Meals: Bless food as viriditas (the greening that nourishes your body)\r\n- Evening: Journal one place you noticed viriditas today (in nature, in\r\n  relationships, in creative work)\r\n\r\nWEEKLY SUSTAINED PRACTICES:\r\n- Garden or tend plants (even a single houseplant) — literal participation\r\n  in viriditas\r\n- Walk in nature without destination — receptive observation\r\n- Create something (art, music, writing, cooking) — viriditas as generativity\r\n- Practice Hildegard''s herbal remedies or holistic health (viriditas in healing)\r\n\r\nMONTHLY ATTUNEMENT:\r\n- At each new moon or full moon, return to full viriditas meditation (20 min)\r\n- Assess: Where am I greening (alive, growing)? Where am I withering (dry,\r\n  stuck)?\r\n- Adjust: Add practices that restore viriditas where ariditas has crept in\r\n\r\nANTIDOTES TO ARIDITAS (Spiritual Dryness):\r\nIf you feel viriditas has left your life:\r\n- PHYSICALLY: Rest, hydration, nourishing food, time in nature, movement\r\n- SPIRITUALLY: Prayer, music, beauty, community, service\r\n- CREATIVELY: Make something with your hands (no goal, just process)\r\n- RELATIONALLY: Seek life-giving relationships; release draining ones\r\n\r\nHildegard''s Insight:\r\n\"When the soul is dry, it is like land that is not moistened by rain but is\r\nhard and unyielding. But when it is watered, it softens and becomes fruitful.\"\r\n(*Causae et Curae*)\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Expected:** User has concrete daily/weekly/monthly practices to sustain viriditas awareness beyond meditation sessions. Life becomes practice, not just scheduled sessions.\r\n\r\n**On failure:** If integration feels overwhelming, choose ONE daily micro-practice only (morning greeting of green world). Full integration takes months to years; start small.\r\n\r\n## Validation Checklist\r\n\r\n- [ ] User understands viriditas as divine life force, not mere greenness\r\n- [ ] Preparation phase completed (grounding, centering, intention-setting)\r\n- [ ] Core meditation practiced with observation, participation, and integration phases\r\n- [ ] Seasonal variation noted (spring/summer/autumn/winter manifestations)\r\n- [ ] At least one daily or weekly integration practice identified\r\n- [ ] User aware of ariditas (dryness) as opposite of viriditas\r\n- [ ] Practice framed as contemplative participation, not goal-driven achievement\r\n\r\n## Common Pitfalls\r\n\r\n1. **Romanticizing Nature**: Viriditas includes decay, death, and composting — not just pretty flowers\r\n2. **Seasonal Rigidity**: Winter is not \"bad\" or \"less green\" — it is necessary rest before spring\r\n3. **Indoor Dismissal**: If unable to access nature, indoor practice is valid. Hildegard spent much time in cloistered convent\r\n4. **Productivity Lens**: Viriditas is not about \"doing more\" — it is about BEING alive and generative in one''s proper season\r\n5. **Ignoring Ariditas**: Denying spiritual dryness prevents addressing it. Name it, then practice restoration\r\n6. **Solo Practice Only**: Viriditas is communal. Hildegard lived in a community of nuns. Share practice with others when possible\r\n7. **Theological Avoidance**: Viriditas is theological (Holy Spirit), not secular ecology. The spiritual dimension is integral to Hildegard''s concept\r\n\r\n## Related Skills\r\n\r\n- `formulate-herbal-remedy` — Plants as viriditas; remedies restore greening to the body\r\n- `assess-holistic-health` — Health is viriditas in the body; illness is ariditas\r\n- `compose-sacred-music` — Hildegard''s music is viriditas made audible\r\n- `consult-natural-history` — Physica''s plants, stones, animals all express viriditas\r\n- `meditate` (esoteric domain) — General meditation framework (viriditas is Hildegardian variant)\r\n- `heal` (esoteric domain) — Healing restores viriditas to body and soul\r\n- `cultivate-bonsai` (gardening domain) — Bonsai care as literal participation in viriditas\r\n- `plan-garden-calendar` (gardening domain) — Seasonal attunement through gardening\r\n"},"lastSynced":"2026-03-08T02:14:02.689Z","agentAnalysis":{"suitability":{"en":"Ideal for Mindfulness Agents seeking to integrate Hildegardian contemplative spirituality and philosophical meditation practices into their workflows.","zh":"适合于寻求将希尔德加德神修灵修和哲学冥想实践整合到工作流程中的正念代理。","ja":"ヒルデガルド神修の瞑想的精神性と哲学的瞑想の実践をワークフローに統合しようとするマインドフルネス エージェントに適しています。","ko":"힐데가르드의 명상적 영성과 철학적 명상 실습을 워크플로에 통합하려는 마음챙김 에이전트에게 적합합니다.","es":"Ideal para Agentes de Mindfulness que buscan integrar la espiritualidad contemplativa hildegardiana y las prácticas de meditación filosófica en sus flujos de trabajo.","fr":"Idéal pour les agents de pleine conscience cherchant à intégrer la spiritualité contemplative hildegardienne et les pratiques de méditation philosophique dans leurs flux de travail.","de":"Ideal für Mindfulness-Agents, die die hildegardianische kontemplative Spiritualität und philosophische Meditationspraktiken in ihre Workflows integrieren möchten.","pt":"Ideal para Agentes de Mindfulness que buscam integrar a espiritualidade contemplativa hildegardiana e práticas de meditação filosófica em seus fluxos de trabalho.","ru":"Идеально для агентов осознанности, стремящихся интегрировать гильдегардианскую созерцательную духовность и философские практики медитации в свои рабочие процессы.","ar":"مثالية للوكلاء الذين يبحثون عن دمج الروحانية التأملية هيلديغاردية وممارسات التأمل الفلسفي في تدفقات العمل الخاصة بهم."},"recommendation":{"en":"Empowers agents to guide users through meditation and philosophical contemplation on viriditas, leveraging Claude Code integration for a holistic approach to coding and spirituality, while utilizing WSL-Windows environments for seamless development.","zh":"赋予代理引导用户通过冥想和哲学沉思viriditas，利用Claude Code集成实现编码和灵性的整体方法，同时利用WSL-Windows环境实现无缝开发。","ja":"エージェントは、Claude Codeの統合を利用してviriditasについての瞑想と哲学的沈思をユーザーに導き、WSL-Windows環境を使用して開発をスムーズに行うことができます。","ko":"에이전트가 사용자를 명상과 철학적沈思의 viriditas를 통해 안내할 수 있도록 하며, Claude Code 통합을 통해 코딩과 영성의 종합적 접근을 구현하고, WSL-Windows 환경을 사용하여 개발을 무중단으로 진행할 수 있습니다.","es":"Permite a los agentes guiar a los usuarios a través de la meditación y la contemplación filosófica sobre la viriditas, aprovechando la integración de Claude Code para un enfoque holístico de la codificación y la espiritualidad, mientras utiliza entornos WSL-Windows para un desarrollo sin problemas.","fr":"Permet aux agents de guider les utilisateurs à travers la méditation et la contemplation philosophique sur la viriditas, en exploitant l''intégration de Claude Code pour une approche holistique de la codification et de la spiritualité, tout en utilisant des environnements WSL-Windows pour un développement sans problème.","de":"Ermächtigt Agenten, Benutzer durch Meditation und philosophische Kontemplation über die Viriditas zu führen, indem es die Claude Code-Integration für einen holistischen Ansatz zur Codierung und Spiritualität nutzt, während es WSL-Windows-Umgebungen für eine reibungslose Entwicklung verwendet.","pt":"Habilita os agentes a orientar os usuários por meio da meditação e contemplação filosófica sobre a viriditas, aproveitando a integração do Claude Code para uma abordagem holística de codificação e espiritualidade, enquanto utiliza ambientes WSL-Windows para desenvolvimento sem interrupções.","ru":"Наделяет агентов возможностью руководить пользователями через медитацию и философское созерцание о viriditas, используя интеграцию с Claude Code для комплексного подхода к программированию и духовности, а также используя среды WSL-Windows для бесперебойной разработки.","ar":"تمكّن الوكلاء من توجيه المستخدمين من خلال التأمل والتأمل الفلسفي حول الفيرديتاس، مستفيدة من تكامل كلود كود لنهج شمولي للبرمجة والروحانية، في حين استخدام بيئات ويسل-ويندوز للتنمية دون انقطاع."},"useCases":{"en":["Guiding users through Hildegardian contemplative spirituality practices","Developing meditation guides that integrate body, earth, and spirit","Creating coding tutorials that incorporate philosophical contemplation on viriditas"],"zh":["引导用户进行希尔德加德神修的瞑想实践","开发整合身体、地球和灵魂的冥想指南","创建包含viriditas哲学沉思的编码教程"],"ja":["ヒルデガルド神修の瞑想的実践をユーザーに導く","身体、地球、霊魂を統合した瞑想ガイドを開発する","viriditasの哲学的沈思を含むコーディングチュートリアルを作成する"],"ko":["힐데가르드의 명상적 영성 실습을 사용자에게 안내하는 것","신체, 지구, 영혼을 통합한 명상 가이드 개발","viriditas의 철학적沈思를 포함한 코딩 튜토리얼 생성"],"es":["Guiar a los usuarios a través de prácticas de espiritualidad contemplativa hildegardiana","Desarrollar guías de meditación que integren el cuerpo, la tierra y el espíritu","Crear tutoriales de codificación que incorporen la contemplación filosófica sobre la viriditas"],"fr":["Guider les utilisateurs à travers les pratiques de spiritualité contemplative hildegardienne","Développer des guides de méditation qui intègrent le corps, la terre et l''esprit","Créer des didacticiels de codage qui intègrent la contemplation philosophique sur la viriditas"],"de":["Benutzer durch hildegardianische kontemplative Spiritualitätspraktiken führen","Meditationsleitfäden entwickeln, die Körper, Erde und Geist integrieren","Codingleitfäden erstellen, die philosophische Kontemplation über die Viriditas einbeziehen"],"pt":["Orientar os usuários por meio de práticas de espiritualidade contemplativa hildegardiana","Desenvolver guias de meditação que integram corpo, terra e espírito","Criar tutoriais de codificação que incorporam contemplação filosófica sobre a viriditas"],"ru":["Руководить пользователями через практики гильдегардианской созерцательной духовности","Разрабатывать руководства по медитации, которые интегрируют тело, землю и дух","Создавать учебные пособия по программированию, которые включают философское созерцание о viriditas"],"ar":["توجيه المستخدمين من خلال ممارسات الروحانية التأملية هيلديغاردية","تطوير أدلة التأمل التي تدمج الجسد والتربة والروح","إنشاء دروس برمجة تضم التأمل الفلسفي حول الفيرديتاس"]},"limitations":{"en":["Requires Claude Code integration","WSL-Windows environment necessary for development","Focused on Hildegardian contemplative spirituality, may not be suitable for other meditation practices"],"zh":["需要Claude Code集成","需要WSL-Windows环境进行开发","专注于希尔德加德神修的瞑想灵修，可能不适合其他的冥想实践"],"ja":["Claude Codeの統合が必要","WSL-Windows環境が開発に必要","ヒルデガルド神修の瞑想的霊修に焦点を当てているため、他の瞑想実践には適さない可能性がある"],"ko":["Claude Code 통합이 필요","WSL-Windows 환경이 개발에 필요","힐데가르드의 명상적 영성에 초점을 둔ため, 다른 명상 실습에는 적합하지 않을 수 있음"],"es":["Requiere integración de Claude Code","Entorno WSL-Windows necesario para el desarrollo","Centrado en la espiritualidad contemplativa hildegardiana, puede no ser adecuado para otras prácticas de meditación"],"fr":["Nécessite l''intégration de Claude Code","Environnement WSL-Windows nécessaire pour le développement","Axé sur la spiritualité contemplative hildegardienne, peut ne pas convenir aux autres pratiques de méditation"],"de":["Benötigt Claude Code-Integration","WSL-Windows-Umgebung erforderlich für die Entwicklung","Konzentriert sich auf die hildegardianische kontemplative Spiritualität, kann für andere Meditationspraktiken nicht geeignet sein"],"pt":["Exige integração do Claude Code","Ambiente WSL-Windows necessário para desenvolvimento","Focado em espiritualidade contemplativa hildegardiana, pode não ser adequado para outras práticas de meditação"],"ru":["Требует интеграции с Claude Code","Среда WSL-Windows необходима для разработки","Сосредоточен на гильдегардианской созерцательной духовности, может быть не подходит для других практик медитации"],"ar":["يتطلب تكامل كلود كود","بيئة ويسل-ويندوز ضرورية للتنمية","يركز على الروحانية التأملية هيلديغاردية، قد لا تكون مناسبة لطرق التأمل الأخرى"]},"version":4},"contentHash":"6e58df35e662ed54fea3cd39c77bb18f9ce5ed8f7ce235f7c5dedb49dd4fa843","qualityScore":61}');
